  "problem": "Consider the path $C,$ in the plane, as the boundary of the region enclosed by the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ and the region $D$ bounded by $C.$ According to Green's theorem, \n\n$$\n{\u222e}_{C}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}\u20612y\\,dx+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}\u20612y\\,dy={\u222c}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is traversed counterclockwise. Calculate the function $f(x,y).$",
